        "title": "A Bit Trying for Tourists",
        "text": "I love this comples of ancient temples dedicated to Shiva as \"lord of animals\" - so much jungle & so many monkeys - tourists aren't allowed in most of the temples (discrimination) & he over zealous gaurds will try to force you to pay 1000 pupees ($10) to just walk onto the premises. You can always go through the jungle paths to avoid the fees, but it's still a bit of a search to find the best places to see there- I recommend going off the trails into the Sleshmantak jungles & also sitting at the Sri Goraknath temple at the very top of the hill. The babas (Hindu renunciates) there wear huge earrings through the center of their ears which supposedly opens a psychic channel. ",
